---
description: Use stemmed arrows in UI icons — never bare chevrons (< > ^)
alwaysApply: true
---

# No chevron icons

Do not use bare chevron shapes for navigation or direction in UI — no `<`, `>`, `^`, `‹`, `›`, or V-shaped polylines without a stem.

## Use instead

| Instead of | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Chevron up (`^`, polyline-only up V) | Arrow up — vertical stem + arrowhead |
| Chevron down | Arrow down — stem + head |
| Chevron left / right (`<`, `>`) | Arrow left / right — stem + head |
| `polyline` V-shape only | Line/path with shaft and distinct head |

## Arrow icon pattern

```tsx
// Up — stem + head, not a lone chevron
<line x1="8" y1="13" x2="8" y2="5" />
<line x1="5" y1="8" x2="8" y2="5" />
<line x1="11" y1="8" x2="8" y2="5" />
```

## Scope

- Icons, buttons, nav affordances, carousel controls, accordions
- Inline UI glyphs in components

Prose arrows in copy (e.g. `→` in a link label) are fine when they read as text, not as icon substitutes.

When reviewing UI, replace chevron-only SVGs before shipping.
